  "section_notes": "The final text removes automatic market bans and recalls: exceeding 5% in S2 and 8 per 100,000 in S5 triggers only regulator review or assessment, so the Hearth 10 and Ember 8 can keep selling. Per-model failure rates go to purchasers and regulators but not to the public. S1 reporting is quick (24 hours) but covers only serious incidents, leaving minor overheating unreportable. S3 and S4 sit within acceptable ranges, with a 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression deadline."
